# Project Core Rules

CSCI 544 project: paired static/dynamic LLM persona simulations on CGA-WIKI openings, scored by a blind judge and compared to real personal-attack labels. `SPEC.md` is the source of truth; `DECISIONS.md` records what the team has agreed.

## Information flow (never violate)

- Only `src/evaluate.py` may read real labels (`data/processed/labels.jsonl`, `real_outcome`).
- Generator and state updater see only `ConversationSeed` turns and generated turns — never labels or future human turns.
- Judge input is ordered dialogue text plus the rubric only. No condition name, trust values, model provenance, or labels.
- Static and dynamic runs share seed, personas, model, turn budget, and generation settings. Only the update policy differs.

## Where things live

- Shared types come from `src/schemas.py`. Do not redefine `DialogueTurn`, `AgentState`, etc. in other modules.
- One module per owner in `src/`; don't edit another owner's module without saying so.
- Tunable parameters go in `configs/*.yaml`, prompt text in `prompts/*_vN.txt`. No hardcoded prompts or magic numbers in code.
- Entry points live in `scripts/`; `src/` modules don't run anything on import.
- Notebooks are for exploration only; anything the pipeline depends on belongs in `src/` or `scripts/`.

## Safety and reproducibility

- Never commit or log API keys; read them from `.env` via environment variables.
- Never commit `data/raw/`, `data/processed/`, or `outputs/`.
- Log failed runs with a status and error; never silently drop them.
- Record model id, prompt version, updater version, and random seed in `run_metadata`.
- Pin new dependencies in `requirements.txt` as `name==version`. Target Python 3.13.
